  <section>
    <section class="check-understanding">
      <exercise data-content-id="2db26d10-04e4-4540-a272-30228d06b376">
        <problem>
          <para>
      <para>Here is a graph of \(p\), an insect population, \(w\) weeks after it was first measured. The population
          grows exponentially. 
          <figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/be8f4718ec44f2071d0a890cab99468e1bc5a1c2"/></media></figure><para>
              What is the weekly factor of growth for the insect population? </para>
          </para>
      </para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>3</para>
          <para>
      <para>The correct answer is 3.
      </para>
    </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </section>
